<section class="fragment-review" data-artifact="review" data-rev="1">
<style>
.fragment-review { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 860px; }
.fr-heatmap { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin: 12px 0; }
.fr-chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; }
.fr-chip-clean { background: #d1fae5; color: #065f46; }
.fr-chip-caveats { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; }
.fr-chip-no { background: #fee2e2; color: #991b1b; }
.fr-sev-bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin: 10px 0; font-size: 13px; }
.fr-sev { padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: 600; }
.fr-sev-high { background: #fde68a; color: #78350f; }
.fr-sev-low { background: #e0e7ff; color: #3730a3; }
.fr-sev-nit { background: #f3f4f6; color: #374151; }
.fr-findings { margin-top: 16px; }
.fr-finding { border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 10px; overflow: hidden; }
.fr-finding-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; background: #f9fafb; cursor: pointer; user-select: none; }
.fr-finding-header:hover { background: #f1f5f9; }
.fr-badge { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.fr-badge-high { background: #fde68a; color: #78350f; }
.fr-badge-low { background: #e0e7ff; color: #3730a3; }
.fr-badge-nit { background: #f3f4f6; color: #374151; }
.fr-badge-deferred { background: #fef9c3; color: #713f12; }
.fr-finding-body { padding: 12px 14px; border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb; display: none; font-size: 13px; }
.fr-finding-body.open { display: block; }
.fr-finding-body code { background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2px 5px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 12px; }
.fr-finding-body pre { background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 12px; }
.fr-meta { font-size: 11px; color: #6b7280; margin-top: 6px; }
</style>

<div class="fr-heatmap">
  <span class="fr-chip fr-chip-caveats">correctness — fixed</span>
  <span class="fr-chip fr-chip-caveats">reliability — 1 HIGH deferred</span>
  <span class="fr-chip fr-chip-clean">security — clean</span>
  <span class="fr-chip fr-chip-clean">testing — 1 LOW deferred</span>
  <span class="fr-chip fr-chip-clean">maintainability — clean</span>
  <span class="fr-chip fr-chip-clean">code-simplification — deferred</span>
  <span class="fr-chip fr-chip-clean">docs — 1 LOW deferred</span>
  <span class="fr-chip fr-chip-clean">release — clean</span>
</div>

<div class="fr-sev-bar">
  <span>Open findings:</span>
  <span class="fr-sev fr-sev-high">HIGH 1</span>
  <span class="fr-sev fr-sev-low">LOW 2</span>
  <span class="fr-sev fr-sev-nit">NIT 1</span>
</div>

<div class="fr-findings">

  <div class="fr-finding">
    <div class="fr-finding-header" onclick="(function(h){const b=h.nextElementSibling;b.classList.toggle('open');})(this)">
      <span class="fr-badge fr-badge-high">HIGH</span>
      <span class="fr-badge fr-badge-deferred">DEFERRED</span>
      <strong>CR-2</strong>
      <span style="flex:1">projectionVersion polling busy-loop — idle CPU at ~60 polls/second</span>
      <span style="font-size:11px;color:#6b7280">reliability</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fr-finding-body">
      <p><strong>Location:</strong> <code>IsometricScene.kt:148</code></p>
      <pre>while (true) {
    delay(16L)  // runs forever on idle scenes
    val current = engine.projectionVersion
    if (current != lastVersion) { sceneVersion++ }
}</pre>
      <p><strong>Issue:</strong> The projection-version bridge polls every 16ms regardless of engine changes.
      On a long-lived scene with a static engine this loop runs indefinitely at ~60 polls/second.</p>
      <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Expose a <code>Flow&lt;Int&gt;</code> / <code>StateFlow&lt;Int&gt;</code> from <code>IsometricEngine</code>,
      or use <code>snapshotFlow { engine.projectionVersion }</code> if the field becomes Compose-observable.</p>
      <div class="fr-meta">surfaced 2026-07-07 · pre-existing: false · confidence: med</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fr-finding">
    <div class="fr-finding-header" onclick="(function(h){const b=h.nextElementSibling;b.classList.toggle('open');})(this)">
      <span class="fr-badge fr-badge-low">LOW</span>
      <span class="fr-badge fr-badge-deferred">DEFERRED</span>
      <strong>TST-1</strong>
      <span style="flex:1">Drag-within-window test has vacuous assertion</span>
      <span style="font-size:11px;color:#6b7280">testing</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fr-finding-body">
      <p><strong>Location:</strong> <code>DoubleTapDisambiguationTest.kt:170</code></p>
      <pre>assertThat(singleTaps).isEqualTo(0)
assertThat(doubleTaps).isEqualTo(0)
// no code exercised above — trivially true from the start</pre>
      <p><strong>Issue:</strong> The test asserts two counters start at zero before exercising any code path. Cannot fail even if drag callbacks fired incorrectly.</p>
      <div class="fr-meta">surfaced 2026-07-07 · pre-existing: false · confidence: med</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fr-finding">
    <div class="fr-finding-header" onclick="(function(h){const b=h.nextElementSibling;b.classList.toggle('open');})(this)">
      <span class="fr-badge fr-badge-low">LOW</span>
      <span class="fr-badge fr-badge-deferred">DEFERRED</span>
      <strong>DOCS-1</strong>
      <span style="flex:1">NodeDragState feature lacks end-to-end how-to guide</span>
      <span style="font-size:11px;color:#6b7280">docs</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fr-finding-body">
      <p><strong>Location:</strong> <code>CHANGELOG.md:22</code></p>
      <p><strong>Issue:</strong> <code>NodeDragState</code> / <code>rememberNodeDragState</code> / <code>NodeDragBounds</code> appear in the changelog and reference page but have no walkthrough guide for the tap-to-select-then-drag pattern.</p>
      <div class="fr-meta">surfaced 2026-07-07 · pre-existing: false · confidence: low</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fr-finding">
    <div class="fr-finding-header" onclick="(function(h){const b=h.nextElementSibling;b.classList.toggle('open');})(this)">
      <span class="fr-badge fr-badge-nit">NIT</span>
      <span class="fr-badge fr-badge-deferred">DEFERRED</span>
      <strong>CS-2</strong>
      <span style="flex:1">Magic constant delay(16L) has no named symbol</span>
      <span style="font-size:11px;color:#6b7280">code-simplification</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fr-finding-body">
      <p><strong>Location:</strong> <code>IsometricScene.kt:148</code></p>
      <pre>delay(16L) // one frame boundary</pre>
      <p><strong>Fix:</strong> <code>private const val FRAME_POLL_INTERVAL_MS = 16L</code></p>
      <div class="fr-meta">surfaced 2026-07-07 · pre-existing: false · confidence: low</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<script>
(function() {
  window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', {
    detail: { name: 'review', artifact: 'review', counts: { findings: 4, blockers: 0 } }
  }));
})();
</script>
</section>
